  partName: Cylinder Head Bolt (4)
  description: The Cylinder Head Bolt (4) is a small, intricately shaped component
    located at the top-center-center of the engine, made from Material.001. By providing
    additional clamping force to the cylinder head, it contributes to the engine's
    ability to contain high pressures and temperatures, ultimately enhancing performance
    and efficiency. The bolt's tiny size belies its importance, as it plays a vital
    role in maintaining the structural integrity of the engine.
